\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{5}=-\\frac{9}{5}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the amplitude is $|A|.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $A=-\\frac{9}{5}.$ Therefore, the amplitude is $|A|=|-\\frac{9}{5}|=\\frac{9}{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332896 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e616922-3cb9-5d0d-adb4-d5f2e9937e8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330503} {:answer/id #uuid "49dad8f8-1906-5970-a75a-02b096c82478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330613} {:answer/id #uuid "516a2115-a7cd-5bc8-a211-941eb2a6c091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330685} {:answer/id #uuid "806611f0-40df-5c8d-9ad4-4c05dfff9ea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331086} {:answer/id #uuid "becedc42-47cd-5039-8a91-00d39f0721ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "becedc42-47cd-5039-8a91-00d39f0721ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331640} :answer-field/id #uuid "676bbfa2-424e-564f-8cd6-1aa8c4be8621" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332393}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "149ae65f-0d63-59f5-9ea2-35fcac7e5bad" :question/math-academy-id "q-53428" :question/problem "What is the amplitude of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3})?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the amplitude is $|A|.$ \n\nSince $A=1,$ we have that the amplitude is $|A|=|1|=1.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Amplitude of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129122 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128878 :question/id #uuid "7f6626c7-c3d3-5f4e-b2c7-1e9bf07e883c" :question/math-academy-id "e-15610" :question/problem "Calculate the period of the function $y=\\cos(2x).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function in the form $y = A\\cos(Bx +C) + D,$ the period is $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=2.$ Therefore, the period is $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{\\left(2\\right)}=\\pi.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1eeb42af-74ee-53d7-af9f-be171f77968f" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048595 :topic/math-academy-id 784 :topic/title "Horizontal Stretches of Trigonometric Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129782 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1db175ad-694b-5bb9-959a-3d6e0b2057a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327192} {:answer/id #uuid "287568e1-57a3-5493-8522-6c1936081561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327277} {:answer/id #uuid "6b8dcb34-da39-5684-9e5c-886c63a6cb4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327859} {:answer/id #uuid "6bcad715-2c41-5c6c-a271-14ddd1312559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327863} {:answer/id #uuid "94944c92-3dbf-5f11-9056-1700eb82c373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1db175ad-694b-5bb9-959a-3d6e0b2057a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327192} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2a75f1b-46ee-5473-b6c7-6d7a730ef92a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-